      "stop_reason": "end_turn",
      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "Perfect! I have the answer directly from the wiki.\n\n**The Hub keeps the Anthropic API key out of its own process environment by never storing it there in the first place.** According to [[credential-scoping]]:\n\nA local secrets loader reads the API key from a git-ignored \u0060.env\u0060 file at startup and injects it **only into the environment of spawned child processes** (the Ingest agent and Query agent) immediately before they start. The Hub\u0027s own process environment is never mutated with the credential.\n\nThis architecture ensures that even if the Hub process is compromised or misbehaves, it cannot leak the API key simply by inspecting its own environment variables \u2014 the key exists only inside the short-lived child processes that actually need to call the Anthropic API.",
      "input_tokens": 4199,
